# External Services Pack

Use this pack when the project talks to paid APIs, messaging platforms, cloud services, production accounts, or external automation targets.

## Rules

- Do not call paid or production services without explicit approval.
- Do not print or commit API keys, sessions, tokens, cookies, or account metadata.
- Prefer mocks, fakes, local emulators, or dry-run modes for tests.
- Keep dependency, security, and external-service changes separate from feature work.
- Document rate limits, costs, and irreversible operations before running commands.

## Verification

- State whether verification used mocks/local services or real external services.
- Record unverified external-service behavior as residual risk.

